-- Plant reference catalogue · GUIDELINE seed (2026-10-05): the species the FLL guidelines themselves print.
-- Sources (rendered PDFs read in the authoring session, 2026-10-05):
--   FLL-GAR-2023 Tab. 29 „Beispiele von Pflanzen mit aggressiven Wurzeln oder Rhizomen“, § 10.3, printed p. 125 — 30 species
--     (15 printed rows 2–16 × column 1 „Helophyten und Hydrophyten“ / column 2 „Terrestrische Pflanzen“; footnote 1 on Lythrum salicaria).
--     The live regulation_tables TAB29 carries the same 30 rows (scripts/migrations/20260929200000_fll_gar_2023_tables_coverage_block1.sql);
--     the prod read-back of that table was NOT possible in the authoring session (production reads blocked) — the PDF text was read instead.
--   FLL-TP-Rhizom-2023 § 1 Einführung, printed p. 7 (PDF page 8) — the four helophyte test species (Phragmites australis the most aggressive
--     rhizome former; Cyperus longus, Schoenoplectus lacustris, Zizania caduciflora) and the five terrestrial root-test species
--     (Alnus glutinosa, Populus tremula, Pyracantha coccinea 'Orange Charmer', Elymus (=Agropyron) repens, Pleioblastus distichus).
-- Rules: scientific_name = the printed botanical text verbatim; common_name_de = the printed German name; plant_group 'bank_terrestrial'
--   for the printed group „Terrestrische Pflanzen“, otherwise 'other' (the pages do not print a § 10.4.3 group — the printed group is in notes);
--   no depth / light / height — the pages do not print them (columns stay NULL). aggressive_rhizome true for all 30 Tab.-29 species and for the
--   TP helophytes + Elymus / Pleioblastus; false for the three terrestrial root-test species Alnus / Populus / Pyracantha 'Orange Charmer'.
--   A species printed in both sources (Phragmites australis, Zizania caduciflora) is ONE row carrying both references.
-- Expected after apply: 36 rows source_kind 'guideline' · 33 aggressive_rhizome true · 3 false.
-- Idempotent (ON CONFLICT (scientific_name, source_kind) DO UPDATE). Nothing here changes a gate, a field or an FLL value.
-- ORDER: apply AFTER supabase/migrations/20261005180000_plant_catalog.sql.
-- STAGED — not applied. Apply: node scripts/apply-migration.mjs scripts/migrations/20261005181000_plant_catalog_guideline_seed.sql
-- Rollback: scripts/migrations/rollback-20261005181000_plant_catalog_guideline_seed.sql
-- Read-back: node scripts/verification/prod-query.mjs scripts/verification/apply/readback-plant-catalog.sql
BEGIN;
ON CONFLICT (scientific_name, source_kind) DO UPDATE SET
  common_name_de = EXCLUDED.common_name_de, plant_group = EXCLUDED.plant_group, notes = EXCLUDED.notes,
  aggressive_rhizome = EXCLUDED.aggressive_rhizome, aggressive_source = EXCLUDED.aggressive_source,
  source_ref = EXCLUDED.source_ref, licence_status = EXCLUDED.licence_status, active = true;
COMMIT;
